  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Isolated showers south of the Turnpike today give\nway to dry and seasonable weather to end the week. Coastal \nstorm effects still look like they will stay mainly east of PA.\n\nHigh pressure and drier air moving down from the north will  \ndominate the forecast for the next 7 days. A couple isolated \nshowers are possible today, mainly south of the PA Turnpike. \nElsewhere, we'll see decreasing clouds across the north and \nbelow average temperatures areawide.\n\nDry weather persists through the end of the week with\ntemperatures trending a couple degrees warmer each day. We'll \nstart to see high clouds from the coastal low on Friday or even \nbefore then. By this weekend, the coastal low will make its\nclosest approach to PA and eastern PA could see some showers\n(mainly east of US-15). Frequent gusts of 20 to 30 mph are\npossible on Saturday and Sunday as well. Western PA should see\nplentiful sunshine this weekend while eastern PA may be shrouded\nin mid- and high-clouds.",
